<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9033" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνῐμ-άω</span></b> , used by early writers only in
			pres. and impf. (aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνίμησα</span> Hierocl.<i><span class="en">
			p.63.19
		</span></i>
		<i><span class="en">
			A.
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			<u>Phoc.</u>
			18
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>draw up, raise</i>
			water by means of leather straps (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμάντες</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἀπὸ τροχιλιᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					4.3.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hierocl.
			</span></i> l.c.; generally, <i>draw out</i> or <i>up,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλους δόρασι ἀνίμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					4.2.8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eq.</u>
				7.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάδον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.93
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνῑμήθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>Mith.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				1.116
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antig.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				157
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνίμημαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pisc.</u>
					50
				</span></i>
			:— freq. used by later writers in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνιμῶμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Alex.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ προβολῇ φόρτον,</span> of
			an elephant, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				2.13
			</span></i>; of the sun causing evaporation, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				1.35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.197
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				1.13.1
			</span></i>: fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Longus
					1.12
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ησάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.773d
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>VH</u>
				2.42
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			seemingly intr. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑαυτόν</span>),
				<i>get up,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				7.1
			</span></i>.</div>
